items.prompt:
Write out your answer to a trader interview opener, as you would say it. The interviewer says: "Make me a market on the squares on a chessboard, any size." The contract pays £1 per square.

Cover every stage in order:
- what you clarify;
- your fair value and range before calculating, with the reason;
- the calculation;
- your quote and its width, before and after you know the answer;
- what you say if the interviewer buys at your ask before you finish.

Practise it aloud with a partner and time it: about two minutes.
